.SH "NAME"
pcre2_get_startchar \- get the starting character offset
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.sp
.ss \n[.ss]
.nf
.fam C
\fB\&#include\fP \fB<pcre2.h>\fP

\fBPCRE2_SIZE\fP pcre2_get_startchar(\fBpcre2_match_data\fP *\fImatch_data\fP);
.fam
.fi
.ss \n[.ss] 0
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.sp
After a successful call of pcre2_match() that was passed the match block
that is this function\(cqs argument, this function returns the code unit offset of
the character at which the successful match started. For a non\-partial match,
this can be different to the value of \f(CRovector[0]\fP if the pattern contains
the \f(CR\(rsK\fP escape sequence. After a partial match, however, this value is always
the same as \f(CRovector[0]\fP because \f(CR\(rsK\fP does not affect the result of a
partial match.
.sp
There is a complete description of the PCRE2 native API in the
\f(CRpcre2api\fP
page and a description of the POSIX API in the
\f(CRpcre2posix\fP
page.